From 81fb548974265c07dbeb7dc6b3f91f427b5a9722 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 15:56:05 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] Renew leases on their own clock, outside the slow host
 pass

An app-funded renew is valid only inside the owner's renew window (285 s on
minipc) while the serial pass takes ~7 min under public-RPC rate limits, so a
lease got at most one attempt per window; on 2026-10-22 the adapter's one
attempt met a transient lease-gas quorum failure and the lease expired.

Port the Linux supervisor's design (renewLeases/leaseGasRenewDue) to the
Windows host: a 30-s keeper renews due leases of deployments this box serves,
on a fresh ledger row and a fresh host wallet decision, one renewal per
deployment shared with the pass, retried after 60 s, never a claim of an
expired lease and never the operator's ETH. Eligibility is published only
after the pass's serving reconciliation, for the identity the box serves; a
local permit (the decision's deadline, no hold/stop/give-up/withdrawal since)
is re-checked after the lead read and when chain.mjs's operator queue reaches
the send. A release waits for a renewal in flight. The window's lead is read
once per lease per 5 min. A ready row now also requires reconciliation and
keeper eligibility.

(cherry picked from commit 2afa6733fd8a4f45d3049f56fc42c22301752127)
